<title>PHILIPPINES: Meralco eyes rate cut for industrial users.</title>
<headline>Meralco eyes rate cut for industrial users.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Manila Electric Co (Meralco) said it planned to cut the rates imposed on industrial users to lure back companies which have set up their own power generation facilities.</p>
<p>Meralco president Manuel Lopez told reporters that it would cut its rate by 14 to 16 centavos per kilowatt hour as early as June if the Energy Regulatory Board approves its petition.</p>
<p>Power sales to the industrial sector fell by 1.1 percent in 1996, compared to 5.6 percent growth in 1995.</p>
<p>-- MANILA NEWSROOM (63 2) 841-8938 Fax 817-6267</p>
